---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Moving to Andorra from Spain"
  description="A Spanish move to Andorra: the 2001 convention, official permit types on Govern.ad, documents, banks and housing. No invented tax rates."
  path="/moving-to-andorra-from-spain"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Moving from Spain</h1>
    <p>
      The southern road is short. The file is still Andorran. Spain and
      Andorra are separate tax and immigration systems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Official letter codes and Law 2/2026 amounts are on
        <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
        Read
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Govern.ad</a
        >
        and instruct counsel in both jurisdictions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>The 2001 convention</h2>
    <p>
      The Ministry of Justice and Interior publishes a convention of 14
      June 2001 between Andorra, Spain and France on the entry,
      circulation, stay and establishment of their nationals, and on the
      circulation and stay of third-country nationals in Andorra. That
      text is listed on the ministry’s
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/ministeris-i-secretaries-d-estat/ministeri-de-justicia-i-interior/convenis-i-normativa/convenis"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">conventions page</a
      >. It does not replace an immigration authorisation.
    </p>

    <h2>Documents the Government currently describes</h2>
    <p>
      On the
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball/residencia-i-treball-autoritzacio-inicial"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">A.1 initial authorisation</a
      >
      page, nationals of EU and EEA states may present a valid national
      identity card instead of a passport. Spain is an EU member state.
      The rest of the published file still applies: criminal-record
      certificates (apostilled or legalised), accommodation, civil
      status, a contract for workers, and the medical review.
      Self-employed J.1 and residence-without-work D.1 have their own
      lists. Official B.1 is family reunification.
    </p>
    <p>
      Official pages also note that nationals of states with a ratified
      convention may follow a different renewal cycle. Confirm that on
      the renewal page that matches your permit.
    </p>

    <h2>Where people actually live</h2>
    <p>
      Sant Julià de Lòria is the first parish on the road up from Spain.
      The capital and Escaldes sit further up the valley. That is
      geography, not a recommendation. Read the
      <a href="/where-to-live">where to live</a>
      before you instruct a search.
    </p>

    <h2>Tax, banks, property</h2>
    <p>
      Leaving Spanish tax residence is a Spanish question. Andorran tax
      residence is published by the
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/impostos-taxes-i-duana"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Ministeri de Finances</a
      >
      and summarised on
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>
      (183 days or centre of interests, not the D.1 90-day diary). An
      immigration permit is not a substitute for either.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/the-file">Bank accounts</a>,
      <a href="/buying-property">non-resident purchases</a>
      and
      <a href="/become-a-resident">permit types</a>
      are the next notes. Named counsel and agents:
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you are considering a move from Spain."
    source="moving-from-spain"
  />
</Base>
